{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDE3L0hvbmRyb3MlMjAlMjgyMDE3JTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"Hondros","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/eRk9EmZY93TAvBWu5wWz534ISYP.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/7xqX7w755eob2EKHSzLh6iZUjPz.jpg","description":"HONDROS follows the life and career of famous war photographer Chris Hondros by exploring the poignant and often surprising stories behind this award-winning photojournalist's best-known photos. Driven by a commitment to bear witness to the wars of our time after the events of 9/11, Chris was among the first in a new generation of war photographers since Vietnam. HONDROS explores the complexities inherent in covering more than a decade of conflict, while trying to maintain a normal life. It also examines the unknowable calculus involved in making split-second life and death decisions -- before, during and after his photos were made. Chris was killed in Libya in 2011, but he left a lasting impact on his profession that is still felt today.\n\nReleased 2 Mar 2018 · United States of America · Language: English · 86 min\nStudio: Nine Stories Productions, Bold Films, Fox Tale Films\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"2017","genres":["Documentary","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"7.2","runtime":"86 min","cast":["Chris Hondros","Tim Hetherington","Pancho Bernasconi","Greg Campbell","Justin Merriman","Todd Heisler","Mike Kamber","Timothy Fadek"],"director":["Greg Campbell"],"released":"2018-03-02T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Greg Campbell","character":"Director"},{"name":"Chris Hondros","character":"Self (archive footage)"},{"name":"Tim Hetherington","character":"Self (archive footage)","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/qRBQv3Tqg5btMwBFGkr8m1n4jmS.jpg"},{"name":"Pancho Bernasconi","character":"Self"},{"name":"Greg Campbell","character":"Self"},{"name":"Justin Merriman","character":"Self"},{"name":"Todd Heisler","character":"Self